You can't actually get back to the main menu without closing and
reconnecting, but you can edit your configuration from there before
playing next time.

From inside the game, you can use "O", page through the options, and
change "number_pad" -- 0 will use the vi keys, 1 will turn on the ability 
to use the arrow keys on the number pad, and 2 is similar to 1 but "DOS 
compatible", which probably is only meaningful on DOS machines... 
which sporkhack.nineball.org isn't.

I'm not sure of any way to use the standard arrow keys over telnet, as
those transmit something that isn't expected.

